From 29e3f47a8114bd41f52d22ec3445dce6949bd606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 23:08:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui/httpd/rc: v1.2.7 - remove first-boot QIS + EULA consent
 surface, U3 snmp token guard

QIS removal (keep AiMesh wizard, kill EULA modal):
- shared/defaults.c: factory-default x_Setting/w_Setting 0->1 (is_firsttime()
  false -> no NOAUTH first-boot wizard; login demanded immediately; AiMesh
  onboarding requires x_Setting==1 anyway) and pre-sign ASUS_EULA/
  ASUS_NEW_EULA 0->1 (de-clouded build, no consent consumers remain).
- www/state.js: checkPolicy() neutralized (early return) - the blocking
  EULA/PP/TM PolicyUpdateModal read blob-computed EULA_force_sign
  (priv_webapi.o, unauditable) on a 1500ms timer; it can never fire now.
- www/index.asp: first-boot QIS JS redirect removed (also covers upgraded
  boxes with x_Setting=0 persisted).
- QIS_wizard.htm + mobile/js engine + all 9 amas*_page.html KEPT (AiMesh
  Add-Node opens QIS_wizard.htm?flag=amas_addNode); verified in staged fs.

Advanced_Privacy removal (triage 13 remainder, unblocked by the above):
- www/Advanced_Privacy.asp deleted; menuTree tab entry + hide-push removed.
- httpd/web.c: do_set_ASUS_EULA_cgi + set_ASUS_EULA.cgi endpoint removed
  (legacy app-only setter, zero www callers; set_ASUS_NEW_EULA.cgi KEPT for
  the QIS-wizard/AiMesh signing path).

U3 (round-5 logged-unreachable ledger):
- rc/snmpd.c: snmp_sanitize_token() also drops spaces for single-token
  net-snmp directive fields (createUser/rocommunity/rwcommunity) so a spaced
  value cannot shift tokens and silently narrow the ACL; free-text
  sysName/sysLocation/sysContact keep spaces (rest-of-line directives).

Docs: REAPER-FIXES.md round-5 addendum (A5-1..3, U1-U4 ledger) + v1.2.7
surface-removal section; H15/T12 + RELEASE-NOTES mitigation text updated to
the QIS-independent is_passwd_default() login gate.

EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.2.7. Metal tests owed: factory-reset first-boot
(login -> forced password -> dashboard, no QIS/EULA), AiMesh Add-Node
onboarding, node-side onboard edge case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
